From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:01:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] web: pk_words (the last run's words with start/end
 seconds and a confidence, as JSON)

The library already builds a word table for Parakeet: each TDT token carries the
encoder frame it was emitted on and its predicted duration, and words are split on
the SentencePiece marker. A long clip is encoded in windows but decoded once over
the stitched frames, so word times run straight through the window joins. pk-web
only never exposed them. pk_words() returns them on demand as
[{"w","s","e","p"}], p being the lowest token probability in the word.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
